Subject: [PATCH 08541/11362] feat(arc): report LLM-induction latch state;
 gated bounded re-induction on renewed stall

Continues the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review fix pass.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6229 (Gaps finding 2): self.induced is a one-shot latch per
level -- once any attempt fires, induction is structurally unreachable
for the rest of that level, even though a still-stalled agent keeps
accumulating exactly the transition evidence a second attempt would need.
The 400->2000 action-budget raise that makes the wasted tail large enough
to matter was validated on an LLM-off sweep, so this interaction was
never measured.

Ships both halves of the review's suggested fix:

1. Always-on diagnostic, zero behaviour change:
   generator_liveness_witness() now reports induction_tier_latched_off,
   induction_attempt_count, transitions_since_last_induction_attempt, and
   bounded_reinduction_enabled.

2. Gated-off-by-default mechanism: _should_enter_induction gains a
   "renewed_stall_reinduction" branch behind CARNOT_ARC_BOUNDED_REINDUCTION=1,
   resetting the latch once 200 new transitions have accumulated since the
   last attempt (fresh evidence, not a re-ask), capped at 3 attempts per
   level (reset at level boundaries, so the cap is per-level). Gated off
   because a bounded re-attempt's effect on win rate is unmeasured --
   shipping it as a default would repeat the exact mistake Gaps finding 1
   (the dead early-stop-grace flag) already made once, before REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220
   fixed it.

Tests: test_arc_bounded_reinduction_20260808.py (14 tests). Broader
sweep: 73 passed across per-level-reinduction/gate-diagnostics/
liveness-witness/active-probe/plan-start-grid test areas (2
pre-existing, unrelated qat-model-id failures confirmed untouched, per
ops/known-issues.md).

Also acknowledges 13 results/ artifacts flagged stale by the artifact-
freshness-lint. Several declare BOTH arc_competition_agent.py and
arc_executable_world_model.py as dependencies and needed two
acknowledgement entries each: one for this commit's own change, one for
an independent drift on arc_executable_world_model.py caused by the
conductor's own concurrent REQ-ARC-WMTE-6213 commits landing mid-session.
Plus one second-order cascade citing two of the newly-reacknowledged
